      "persona": "Whitehat Hacker",
      "author": "Samira Linton <samira.linton@cyberworld.edu>",
      "subject": "NorthTec Traffic Classification",
      "shortSummary": "Approved business traffic to allow and reconnaissance probes to block.",
      "date": "0001-01-01T00:00:00",
      "body": "Hi {player},\r\n\r\nUse this approved classification for the NorthTec Main Server.\r\n\r\n<b>Allow routine business traffic:</b>\r\n- HTTPS Page Load\r\n- DNS Lookup\r\n- Authenticated User Login\r\n- System Update Check\r\n- Security Gateway Check\r\n- Checkout Request\r\n- Payment Request\r\n- Digitally Signed Email\r\n\r\n<b>Block reconnaissance probes:</b>\r\n- Port Scan\r\n- Host Sweep\r\n- DNS Enumeration\r\n- Directory Enumeration\r\n- Banner Grab\r\n- Vulnerability Scan Probe\r\n- Ping Scan\r\n- Robots.txt Probe\r\n- HTTP Method Probe\r\n\r\nThis classification applies to the current audit scope; production firewall changes require NorthTec’s normal review and testing process.\r\n\r\nSamira",
      "attachements": []
    }
  ]
}
